---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Character Builder
section: Mechanics
summary: >-
  Build a starting Numina character step by step, priced from the skill tables
  as this site has them — and told plainly what the rulebook leaves unpriced.
cardsheet: true
---
{#- The picker over src/js/build-rules.js. The ten sections below are the
    chapter's ten steps; their bodies are rendered by src/js/build-view.js from
    skills.json, which is inlined at the foot of the page as two JSON islands
    (the records, and each skill id's anchor URL from the same map the chapter
    rows get theirs from). Nothing here restates a rule: what each step lists
    is what offered() returns for the build so far.

    Without JS the form stays hidden and the notice below is what a reader
    gets, with links to the chapter and the lists. -#}
{% set steps = [
  [1, "Choose 1 or 2 Aspects"],
  [2, "Choose 1 Foundation"],
  [3, "Choose 1 Culture"],
  [4, "Choose your one Domain"],
  [5, "Choose up to three Excellencies"],
  [6, "Choose up to two Expressions"],
  [7, "Purchase Skills"],
  [8, "Purchase Prowess, Fortitude and Insight"],
  [9, "Purchase Purpose"],
  [10, "Purchase Vitality"]
] %}
<div class="shell">
  {% include "partials/sidebar.njk" %}
  <main class="builder-page" data-pagefind-body data-pagefind-meta="section:Mechanics" data-autolink="off">
    <p class="crumb"><a href="/mechanics/">Mechanics</a></p>
    <h1>Character Builder</h1>
    <p class="lede">{{ summary }}</p>
    <p class="builder__unofficial"><strong>Unofficial.</strong> This page is a player's reading of
    <a href="/mechanics/building-a-character/">Building a Character</a> and the skill chapters, not a
    Staff tool. It prices only what the rulebook prints a number for: the cost to raise Prowess,
    Insight, Fortitude or Vitality is "Cost of next attribute" in the book's own chart, so a build
    that raises them is shown as a floor, never a total. Character approval is a conversation with
    Staff, and this page cannot have it for you.</p>

    <p data-builder-needs-js>The builder needs JavaScript. Without it, the ten steps are in
    <a href="/mechanics/building-a-character/">Building a Character</a> and every skill is in
    <a href="/mechanics/skills/all-skills/">All Skills</a>.</p>

    <div class="builder" data-builder hidden>
      <div class="builder__bar">
        <p class="builder__summary" data-summary aria-live="polite"></p>
        <p class="builder__actions">
          <button type="button" class="builder__button" data-reset>Start over</button>
        </p>
      </div>

      <form class="builder__form" autocomplete="off">
        {%- for step in steps %}
        <section class="builder__step" id="step-{{ step[0] }}" data-step="{{ step[0] }}">
          <h2>Step {{ step[0] }} — {{ step[1] }}</h2>
          {%- if step[0] == 5 %}
          <p class="builder__note">Your first Excellency costs five CP, each subsequent Excellency costs
          one additional CP. Three is a hard limit, and Excellency purchases must be unlocked in-game.
          The <a href="/mechanics/skills/excellencies/">Excellencies chapter</a> has no list to choose
          from, so type the name Staff will know; a name from
          <a href="/mechanics/skills/hidden-excellencies-expressions/">Hidden Excellencies and Expressions</a>
          is flagged here for Staff approval.</p>
          {%- elif step[0] == 1 %}
          <p class="builder__note">These Aspects do not cost CP. You can purchase a total of 3 Aspect
          skills from your Aspects, and from them only one extra Attribute or Armor increasing
          ability. <a href="/mechanics/skills/aspects/">Aspects</a>.</p>
          {%- elif step[0] == 2 %}
          <p class="builder__note">This Foundation does not cost CP. You can purchase up to 2 Foundation
          skills from your Foundation's own table. <a href="/mechanics/skills/foundations/">Foundations</a>.</p>
          {%- elif step[0] == 3 %}
          <p class="builder__note">This Culture does not cost CP. You can purchase up to 2 Culture skills
          from your Culture. <a href="/mechanics/skills/cultures/">Cultures</a>.</p>
          {%- elif step[0] == 4 %}
          <p class="builder__note">This Domain does not cost CP. Its Determination is included; its
          other skills are bought in step 7. <a href="/mechanics/skills/domains/">Domains</a>.</p>
          {%- elif step[0] == 6 %}
          <p class="builder__note">Your first Expression costs five CP, each subsequent Expression costs
          one additional CP. Two at character creation; a third trades away the third Excellency slot
          and needs an email to Staff. Each Expression's first skill is included.
          <a href="/mechanics/skills/expressions/">Expressions</a>.</p>
          {%- elif step[0] == 7 %}
          <p class="builder__note">Skills come from all the different things you have selected
          previously and also include <a href="/mechanics/skills/open-skills/">Open Skills</a>.</p>
          {%- elif step[0] == 8 %}
          <p class="builder__note">Spend these attributes to use skills. Their cost per point is not
          printed in the rulebook, so this page cannot add them to the total.
          <a href="/mechanics/skills/attributes-vitality/">Attributes &amp; Vitality</a>.</p>
          {%- elif step[0] == 9 %}
          <p class="builder__note">Void and Purpose allow you to refresh your other attributes after
          taking a Short or Long Rest. Void cannot currently be purchased.</p>
          {%- else %}
          <p class="builder__note">Vitality defines how many hits your character can take before they
          fall Unstable. Its cost per point is not printed either.</p>
          {%- endif %}
          <div class="builder__step-problems" data-step-problems="{{ step[0] }}"></div>
          <div class="builder__step-body" data-step-body="{{ step[0] }}"></div>
        </section>
        {%- endfor %}
      </form>

      <section class="builder__verdict-section" id="your-build">
        <h2>Your build</h2>
        <div class="builder__verdict" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></div>
        <h3>Share it</h3>
        <p class="builder__hint">The address of this page is the build. It is also kept in this
        browser, and nowhere else.</p>
        <p class="builder__share">
          <input type="text" readonly data-share aria-label="Link to this build">
          <button type="button" class="builder__button" data-copy>Copy link</button>
        </p>
      </section>

      {#- The printable card. cardsheet: true above puts the body on print.css's
          dense treatment, and print.css hides everything on this page but the
          card, so "Print this card" prints one sheet. -#}
      <section class="builder__card-section" id="your-card">
        <h2>Your card</h2>
        <p class="builder__hint">One sheet to carry to the event: your choices, every skill you have with
        its verbal and what it costs to use, your attributes and the CP line. Printing this page prints
        only the card.</p>
        <p class="print-action"><button type="button" onclick="window.print()">Print this card</button></p>
        <div class="builder__card" data-card></div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
</div>
<script type="application/json" id="numina-skills">{{ skills | jsonIsland | safe }}</script>
<script type="application/json" id="numina-skill-links">{{ skills.skills | skillLinks | jsonIsland | safe }}</script>
<script type="module" src="/js/builder.js"></script>
